-- title:
--   Local coordinate at a smooth point of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A\subseteq L$ a valuation subring which is henselian, proper ($A\neq L$ as a subset) and of rank one in the divisibility form: for all $a,b\in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b\neq 0$ there is $n$ with $b\mid a^{n}$. Let $F$ be a field over $L$ which is essentially of finite type and satisfies `IsCurveOver L F` (every nonzero element of $F$ has a degree-zero divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $\operatorname{ord}_v$ of the element, every place has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one over $F$). Let $X$ be an integral scheme with a proper, flat, locally finitely presented morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and $\varphi\colon F\cong$ the function field of $X$ carrying $a\in A$ to its image under the structure map composed with the germ at the generic point. Let $x\in X$ lie over the closed point of $A$, admit no proper specialisation (any $y$ with $x\rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$), and lie in the smooth locus of `toBase`; let $\eta\in X$ also lie over the closed point, satisfy $\eta\rightsquigarrow x$ and $\eta\neq x$. Let $Fbar$ be a field over the residue field of $A$ and $R$ a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with values in $Fbar$, that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ contracting to $A$ along $L\to F$, together with a surjective ring map $R.\mathrm{residue}$ to $Fbar$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero $f\in F$ has $c\in L$ with $c\cdot f$ integral and of nonzero residue; assume the subring of $F$ underlying $R.\mathrm{integers}$ is the image under $\varphi^{-1}$ of the stalk of $X$ at $\eta$. Put $S:=$ the image under $\varphi^{-1}$ of the stalk of $X$ at $x$, a subring of $F$. Assume: $A$ maps into $S$; $Q$ is a place of $Fbar$ over the residue field of $A$ (a proper valuation subring containing the base, with principal ideals) which is rational, i.e. the residue field of $Q$ is generated by the base residue field; every $f\in S$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ in the valuation subring of $Q$; for $f\in S$ integral for $R$, $f$ is a unit of $S$ if and only if $\operatorname{ord}_Q(R.\mathrm{residue}(f))=0$ and $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)\neq 0$; and $T\in S$ is integral for $R$ with $\operatorname{ord}_Q(R.\mathrm{residue}(T))=1$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon A\to S$ inducing the inclusion $A\subseteq L\to F$, the ring $S$ is local, and $\mathfrak m_S=\iota(\mathfrak m_A)S+TS$, $T\notin \iota(\mathfrak m_A)S$, and the composite $A\to S\to S/\mathfrak m_S$ is surjective.
--
--   This is the statement that a function whose reduction has order one at a rational point of the special fibre is a local coordinate there: at a smooth closed point $x$ of the special fibre of the model, the local ring $S=\mathcal O_{X,x}$ is local with maximal ideal generated by the maximal ideal of the base together with $T$, and with residue field equal to that of $A$. It feeds the construction of sections of the model through $x$ in [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus), and uses that the fibre $S/\mathfrak m_A S$ is a principal ideal domain, as recorded in [`AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.isPrincipalIdealRing_stalk_quotient_map_maximalIdeal_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.SemistableModel.isPrincipalIdealRing_stalk_quotient_map_maximalIdeal_of_mem_smoothLocus).
